{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And in the place of the boil there is a white raised area.</b> For that place is not judged by the signs of normal skin above it, and the same applies to the site of a burn. For although the natural skin that was destroyed by the boil or the burn will never return as before, something resembling skin but not true skin will grow in its place, as stated in the chapter <i>Ba Siman</i>. And so the physicians have reported."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:10.924042261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}